\f0\fs40 \cf0 I need to do a Threat Analysis of AI-based Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) systems. This project has two steps: the first one consists of doing the Threat Analysis with a program called Medini Analyze and then the second step consists of doing the Threat Analysis using an AI engine. The goal of the study is to compare the results of the Threat Analysis given by Medini Analyze and the results given by the AI engines to see how reliable they are.\
I uploaded a general scheme of the architecture (general architecture.jpg) and the scheme realized in Medini Analyze (medini architecture.png). The general architecture contains two levels: the upper level, which is responsible with all the decision-making concerning the ACC system and the lower level, which is responsible with acquiring all the necessary data from the environment and applying the decisions taken by the AI engine. The medini analyze scheme contains: the AI controller module which is the equivalent of the upper level module and the two submodules of the lower level. The perception submodule contains radar, camera and Lidar sensors and the OBU hardware. The actuation module contains the brake and throttle actuators and the AEB hardware. Refer to those and construct the Threat Analysis. Organize the table such as: ID, Name, Assets, To Be Assessed(True/False), Category. Structure it in the same way to the output of the Threat Analysis made with Medini Analyze so that I can draw a direct comparison between the two of them at the end. Reference the STRIDE (Spoofing, Tampering, Repudiation, Information Disclosure, Denial of Service DoS, and elevation of privilege) method.}